Let g be a finite-dimensional Lie algebra over C with Lie–Poisson bracket on g*. For two generic covectors x, a ∈ g*, consider the pencil of skew-symmetric bilinear forms {A_x + λ A_a} on g, where A_ξ(u,v) = ⟨ξ,[u,v]⟩. The Jordan–Kronecker invariants of g are the sizes of the Kronecker blocks and the sizes and eigenvalues of the Jordan blocks appearing in the canonical Jordan–Kronecker decomposition of this pencil at a generic point. Compute the Jordan–Kronecker invariants for the following classes of Lie algebras:

(a) semidirect sums g ⋉_ρ V, where g is a semisimple Lie algebra, ρ: g → End(V) is a finite-dimensional representation, and V is regarded as a commutative ideal;
(b) Borel subalgebras of simple Lie algebras;
(c) parabolic subalgebras of simple Lie algebras;
(d) the centralizers z_g(a) of singular elements a ∈ g, where g is a complex simple Lie algebra;
(e) Lie algebras of small dimension (beyond dimension 5).

